<Layout
	title="About"
	description="About Benedikt Weishaupt and the 360° research project"
	pubDate={new Date('January 01 2025')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		This research project explores digital panoramas as visual infrastructures that organize our perception of space and time. The work examines how 360° media oscillate between promises of totality and systematic gaps.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>Benedikt Weishaupt</strong> is a researcher investigating the intersection of digital media, spatial representation, and algorithmic processes. This blog documents ongoing research into panoramic media forms and their role as contemporary visual infrastructures.
	</p>

	<p>
		The project spans three interconnected areas: the technical construction of panoramic images, their cultural and aesthetic implications, and their function as infrastructural elements in digital environments.
	</p>
</Layout>
